# Planning docs — never commit
*.md

# Security model — deployed via `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules` from
# the LOCAL copy. Untracked because GitHub Pages serves every tracked file at
# the site root: goforge.in/firestore.rules returned 200, handing anyone a map
# of exactly what the rules do and do not allow. Removing it is PROSPECTIVE
# only — 15 revisions are already public and must be assumed known. Canonical
# copy + backups live in ~/Desktop/forge-backups/.
firestore.rules
# ── iOS app (branch: ios-app) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: .gitignore has no inline comments. A trailing "# ..." becomes part of
# the pattern, so "www/  # generated" silently matches nothing. That is exactly
# what happened here and it let the generated www/ tree into git status.
node_modules/
# generated by scripts/build-www.mjs
www/
ios/App/Pods/
# generated: cap sync copies www/ into here
ios/App/App/public/
ios/App/Podfile.lock
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/

# NOTE: build-www.mjs deliberately lives at ios/build-www.mjs, not scripts/.
# scripts/ is ignored wholesale (dev tooling, some carrying prod keys), and a
# negation inside an excluded DIRECTORY is unreachable — git never descends
# into it. Keeping the build script under the tracked ios/ tree is simpler than
# unpicking that rule.

# IDE state, internal design canvases, and admin CLI tooling — none of it
# belongs on a public Pages site. scripts/ was already ignored; these two were
# tracked from before that rule and have been served at goforge.in ever since.
.idea/
*.dc.html
